Installation
1. Clone or download the project
```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/online-retail-customer-segmentation.git
cd online-retail-customer-segmentation
```
2. Create a virtual environment
Windows:
```bash
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\activate
```
macOS or Linux:
```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
```
3. Install packages
```bash
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
```
4. Add the dataset
Copy `Online Retail.xlsx` into the `data` folder.
5. Run the project
```bash
python main.py
```
You may also provide the dataset from another location:
```bash
python main.py --data "C:\path\to\Online Retail.xlsx"
```
Running in PyCharm
Open the project folder in PyCharm.
Create or select a Python virtual environment.
Open the PyCharm terminal and run:
```bash
   python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
   ```
Put `Online Retail.xlsx` in `data/`.
Open `main.py` and click Run.
Outputs
After execution, the `outputs/` folder will contain:
`online_retail_analysis_results.xlsx`
`customer_segments.csv`
`cluster_profiles.csv`
`customer_features.csv`
`cluster_number_evaluation.csv`
`final_model_evaluation.csv`
`analysis_summary.txt`
`analysis.log`
charts in `outputs/charts/`
the model bundle in `outputs/models/`
Generated outputs are ignored by Git because they can be recreated by running the analysis.
Documentation
The full six-page visual report is available at:
```text
docs/Online_Retail_Analysis_Report.docx
```
Important data and privacy note
Do not commit customer datasets, credentials, access tokens, `.env` files, or generated files containing confidential information. The provided `.gitignore` excludes the raw Excel dataset, PyCharm settings, virtual environments, generated outputs, and model files.
Limitations
A substantial number of transaction lines do not contain CustomerID values.
The dataset covers slightly more than one year.
Revenue is heavily concentrated in the United Kingdom.
The dataset does not include customer demographics, campaign response, marketing channels, or profit margins.
The cluster quality is moderate, so business effectiveness should be validated through campaign experiments and regular model refreshes.
Future improvements
Add customer lifetime value and churn-risk modelling.
Compare K-Means with hierarchical clustering, Gaussian mixture models, and DBSCAN.
Build a Streamlit dashboard for interactive segment exploration.
Connect the segment assignments to a CRM or campaign-management platform.
Track segment movement and campaign performance over time.
